From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:06:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip64-7.3: fix RK3568 PCIe Root Port reset loop

RK3568 boards with NVMe (Odroid M1) loop in Root Port reset on edge 7.3
and never mount the rootfs. The 7.3 link-down recovery resets the Root
Port on every LINK_REQ_RST_NOT interrupt; the reset re-raises that
interrupt after the link is already up, so recovery repeats forever.

Recover only when the link is genuinely down. Keep the feature.

Tested on: Odroid M1 (RK3568) with NVMe, edge 7.3.0-rc6. Boots to login,
nvme0n1 enumerates, zero Root Port resets.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
index af26a07..2f32540 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
@@ -658,9 +658,20 @@ static irqreturn_t rockchip_pcie_rc_sys_irq_thread(int irq, void *arg)
 
 	if (reg & PCIE_LINK_REQ_RST_NOT_INT) {
 		dev_dbg(dev, "hot reset or link-down reset\n");
-		for_each_pci_bridge(port, pp->bridge->bus) {
-			if (pci_pcie_type(port) == PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
-				pci_host_handle_link_down(port);
+		/*
+		 * reset_root_port() recovers the link by asserting the
+		 * controller reset, which itself re-raises LINK_REQ_RST_NOT
+		 * once the link retrains. On RK3568 that self-induced event is
+		 * delivered after the link is already back up, so acting on it
+		 * resets the Root Port again and loops forever. Only recover
+		 * when the link is actually down, mirroring the link_up() check
+		 * the endpoint IRQ thread already uses.
+		 */
+		if (!rockchip_pcie_link_up(pci)) {
+			for_each_pci_bridge(port, pp->bridge->bus) {
+				if (pci_pcie_type(port) == PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
+					pci_host_handle_link_down(port);
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
